0,Sardinians - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinians,"3 weeks ago - Other native languages are Sassarese, which is rooted in the medieval Tuscan dialect; Gallurese, which is closely related to Corsican; and Tabarchino, a dialect of Ligurian (Genoese). Not much can be gathered from the classical literature about the origins of the Sardinian people. The ethnonym ""S(a)rd"" may belong to the Pre-Indo-European ...","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
1,Music of Sardinia - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_of_Sardinia,"April 23, 2026 - Sardinia is probably the most culturally distinct of all the regions in Italy and, musically, is best known for the tenore polyphonic singing, sacred chants called gosos, the launeddas, an ancient instrument that consists of a set of three single-reed pipes, all three mouth-blown simultaneously ...","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
2,Sardinian language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sardinian_language,"1 week ago - Francesco Gemelli, in Il Rifiorimento ... della Sardegna for a more meticulous analysis of ""the character of the Sardinian language (""indole della lingua sarda"") and the main differences between Sassarese and Tuscan"": ""five languages are spoken in Sardinia, that is Spanish, Italian, ...","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
3,"Sardinian Language And Music | Gabbiano Azzurro Hotel & Suites - Sardinia, Golfo Aranci",https://www.hotelgabbianoazzurro.com/en/Blog/Sardinian-Language-And-Music,"In Sardinia, five native languages are spoken, besides Italian: Sardinian or limba Sarda, in its two varieties Logudorese in the centre and Campidanese in the south; Gallurese which is the Corsican language, in the north; Catalan in Alghero and Ligurian in Carloforte and Calasetta. Sardinian belongs to the romance group of Indo-European languages and is considered autonomous and classified as an idiom standing alone, so much so that since 1997 the regional law recognizes to the Sardinian language equal dignity as to Italian.","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
4,"Sardinian, Sassarese Language (SDC) – L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level & Official Use | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/sdc/,"Sassarese Sardinian is an endangered indigenous language of Italy. It belongs to the Indo-European language family and is part of the Sardinian macrolanguage. The language is used as a first language by all adults in the ethnic community, but not all young people.","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
5,Endangered Languages Project - Sassarese Sardinian - Guide,https://endangeredlanguages.com/lang/5361/guide,"[aka Sardinian, Sardinian, Sassarese, Northwestern Sardinian] Classification: Indo-European · · at risk · Sort by: Recently Added | Best Rated | Most Viewed · delete · Interview to Gian Paolo Bazzoni - Literadura Sarda · 1 · View more video samples · Imparamus su Sardu - Sassarese document ·","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
6,"The launeddas & others, Sardinia in music | SardegnaTurismo - Sito ufficiale del turismo della Regione Sardegna",https://www.sardegnaturismo.it/en/launeddas-others-sardinia-music,"May 7, 2024 - One certainty is that the launeddas have been a part of tradition in numerous central-southern Sardinian villages since the 17th century, particularly Cabras, San Vito, Villaputzu and the villages of the Trexenta region.","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
7,Sardinian & Corsican Folk lyrics with translations,https://lyricstranslate.com/en/sardinian-folk-lyrics.html,"Sardinian & Corsican Folk lyrics: 43 songs translated 120 times to 14 languages. Popular songs: Terra Corsa, Trallallera - Su pobiddu e sa pobidda.","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
8,Endangered Languages Project - Sassarese Sardinian,https://www.endangeredlanguages.com/lang/5361,"[aka Sardinian, Sardinian, Sassarese, Northwestern Sardinian] Classification: Indo-European · · at risk · Compare Sources (2) Information from: “Ethnologue: Languages of the World, 16th Edition (2009)” . M. Paul Lewis · SIL International · Information from: “Ethnologue: Languages of the World, 16th Edition (2009)” .","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
9,Sardinian people facts for kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Sardinian_people,"The mastruca, a sleeveless leather jacket made from sheep or goatskin, is especially linked to Sardinians. Ancient writers like Cicero even called Sardinians ""Sardinians with rough wool cloaks."" Sardinia has its own unique food and music. A map showing genetic links between European and Mediterranean groups.","Sardinian, Sassarese",Indo-European
